<section class="section rule-top">
  <div class="container-edit section-inner">
    <p class="section-label">Mission</p>
    <h2 class="display-section">
      Bring the last non-Dart layer into Dart.
    </h2>

    <div class="mission-grid">
      <article class="mission-card">
        <h3 class="mission-card-title">UI and server are already Dart</h3>
        <p>
          Flutter handles the UI. Cloud Functions and Cloud Run services run your
          Dart. For teams already centered on Dart, infrastructure is often the
          one layer still outside your repo&nbsp;&mdash; carried in HCL and manual
          console work, separate from the language your app, tests, and refactors
          already share.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="mission-card">
        <h3 class="mission-card-title">Terraform&rsquo;s surface, absorbed</h3>
        <p>
          TerraDart is not a parallel runtime. It is Terraform&rsquo;s authoring
          model expressed as Dart factories and sealed types, synthesized to
          standard JSON for the provider you already use.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="mission-card">
        <h3 class="mission-card-title">Discipline by design</h3>
        <p>
          Fixed-value fields become enums. Exactly-one-of blocks become sealed
          classes. Plain <code>Stack</code> subclasses&nbsp;&mdash; loops,
          config, and refactors work the way Dart already does.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
